config BR2_PACKAGE_JETHUB_OLED
	bool "jethub-oled"
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_PYTHON3
	select BR2_PACKAGE_PYTHON_PILLOW # runtime
	select BR2_PACKAGE_FREETYPE # runtime, TrueType in Pillow
	select BR2_PACKAGE_DEJAVU # runtime
	select BR2_PACKAGE_DEJAVU_MONO # runtime, clock digits
	select BR2_PACKAGE_DEJAVU_SANS # runtime, screen headers
	select BR2_PACKAGE_DEJAVU_SANS_CONDENSED # runtime, everything else
	help
	  Status screens and a joystick menu on the SSD1306 OLED of
	  JetHub J310: CPU and RAM rings with temperature and uptime,
	  the IP address, a clock, Ethernet and Wi-Fi details (through
	  nmcli) and reboot. Drawn with Pillow through the ssd1307fb
	  framebuffer.

	  A badge on the resources screen shows whether Home Assistant
	  Core is starting, ready or failing, read from Core over the
	  Unix socket it opens for Supervisor.

	  Also installs the boot logo overlay jethub-oled-splash.dtbo,
	  which ssd1307fb shows from probe until the daemon starts.
